THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
===============================================================================

oshal is original work. Three qualifications, stated so that nobody has to
guess what is carried here and what is not:

  * Runtime dependencies are NOT redistributed by this repository.
    node_modules/ is untracked; every dependency is fetched from its own
    registry, under its own license, at install time. This repository
    therefore carries no notice obligation for them.

  * The agent harnesses are INVOKED, not vendored. Cline, OpenAI Codex CLI,
    Anthropic Claude Code, and Google Gemini CLI are launched as external
    subprocesses by the adapters in
    src/features/llm-provider/services/ and any-bot/server/services/llm/.
    Those adapters are original code that shells out to a CLI the operator
    installs and authenticates themselves. None of the upstream harness
    source is present in this tree, so no upstream notice travels with it.

  * The speaker-diarization service vendors no source either — its container
    downloads checksum-pinned model artifacts published upstream. Its
    attributions, including the upstream license texts, are kept at
    services/speaker-diarization/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

If you vendor third-party source into this tree, it must be
AGPL-compatible and it must be recorded here in the same change. MIT and
Apache-2.0 flow one way into AGPL with their notices retained; proprietary or
EULA-governed code does not flow in at all.
